d an uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot. The key thing I'm thinking through now is what the \"best case\" scenario looks like for the paper: if CIVO replicates cleanly across these environments and the gradient mechanism holds up, that's the narrative I want to support. For Cheetah Run specifically, I'm predicting the baseline should land around 800-850 (which aligns with what I'm already seeing), and I expect the CIVO trigger to show an NVE around 1.6.\n\nNow I'm working through the other environments. Cartpole Swingup should follow a similar pattern—baseline in the 800-870 range, CIVO triggering NVE above 1.5x with collapse in some seeds, while the no dt_emb variant stays stable. For the ManiSkill3 PickCube task, I'm noticing it's mentioned in the tier definition but I need to verify whether the actual experiments are in my plan list or if they're running separately.\n\nLet me organize what I'm actually tracking in the experiment plan versus what's in the registry, then structure the YAML with all the metrics and rationales for the best tier definition. Compiling the full list of planned experiments...\n\nI'm going through the experiment plan systematically and marking which ones have \"planned\" status. So far I've confirmed plans 1 through 10 are done, and now I'm identifying the remaining planned experiments: 11, 12, 13, 14, 20, 21, 22, 23, 30, 31, and 32 all need predictions.\n\nI notice some of these experiments already have partial data in the registry, particularly plans 11, 12, 14, 15, and 20, so I'll need to account for that when making my predictions under the \"best\" tier.\n\nNow I'm organizing the experiments by category—Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Analysis, and Pilots—so I can write detailed predictions with rationales for each one.\n\nFor the Walker Walk experiments, I'm checking the registry data against what we already have. Plan 011 shows both seeds completed with confirmed NVE peaks and collapse patterns, so I can use